  ## 7\. Granola AI: Meetings Without the Pain
  
  **What it does:** Turns meetings into action items automatically
  
  **What it replaces:** Otter.ai ($17/month), meeting assistants, manual note-taking
  
  Meetings are necessary evil. The output matters, but sitting through them? Painful.
  
  Granola AI focuses on what actually matters from meetings:
  
  ✅ Key decisions
  
  ✅ Action items
  
  ✅ Who’s doing what
  
  It doesn’t give you a messy transcript. It gives you **useful information.**
  
  **Perfect for:**
  
  - Regular team calls
  - Client meetings
  - Review sessions
  - Interview debriefs
  
  **The free tier** handles most regular users without needing to upgrade.
  
  **Tip:** Review the action items immediately after the meeting. The AI is good, but quick human verification makes it perfect.
  
  ## 8\. Nano Banana Pro: Images With Actual Text
  
  **What it does:** Generates images with clear, readable text inside them
  
  **What it replaces:** Midjourney ($30/month) for specific use cases
  
  Most AI image generators mess up text. You want a poster with words? You get gibberish.
  
  **Nano Banana Pro nailed this.**
  
  **What you can create:**
  
  - Product mockups with real text
  - Infographics with readable labels
  - Book covers with actual titles
  - Marketing materials with clear messaging
  - Educational diagrams
  - Isometric game assets
  - Technical illustrations
  
  **Real use cases:**
  
  - Digital product covers
  - Social media graphics
  - Presentation visuals
  - YouTube thumbnails
  - Teaching materials
  
  **Example:** I created the cover for my digital playbook entirely with Nano Banana Pro. The text was sharp, the design was professional, and it took 10 minutes instead of hiring a designer.
  
  **Pro tip:** Be specific with text in your prompt. Say exactly what words you want and where.
  
  ## 9\. Canva Magic Studio: Design for Non-Designers
  
  **What it does:** Full AI design system inside Canva
  
  **What it replaces:** Adobe Creative Suite (for most people), separate copywriting tools
  
  Canva stopped being just “templates” a while ago.
  
  **Magic Studio** pulled all their AI features into one place:
  
  - **Magic Write:** Generate content
  - **Magic Design:** Create layouts
  - **Magic Media:** Turn ideas into images/videos (paid feature)
  - **Magic Edit:** Modify images precisely
  - **Magic Grab:** Move elements around intelligently
  - **Magic Animate:** Add motion
  - **Magic Eraser:** Remove backgrounds/objects
  
  **The power combo:**
  
